        "original_id": "fde70bb3-96c5-5f11-aff8-173fb15757aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Othonna, Stangeria eriopus\n- Plant groups: sunflower family, cycads, Stangeriaceae, Bowenia\n- Places: Africa, southern Africa, Australia\n\nFacts:\n- Othonna is a genus of African plants in the sunflower family.\n- Stangeria eriopus is a cycad endemic to southern Africa.\n- Stangeria eriopus is the only species in the genus Stangeria.\n- Stangeria eriopus is most closely related to the Australian genus Bowenia.\n- Stangeria and Bowenia together form the family Stangeriaceae.",
